:\n\n**Key features:**\n- Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to limit concurrency to `max_concurrent` tasks\n- Creates all tasks upfront and gathers them for execution\n- On `KeyboardInterrupt`: catches it, then waits for all pending tasks to finish with `return_exceptions=True` so cleanup code (finally blocks, context manager exits) runs, then re-raises the exception for a clean exit\n\nYou can test it with:\n```python\nfrom run import run_tasks\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def sample_task():\n    try:\n        await asyncio.sleep(10)\n        print(\"Task completed\")\n    finally:\n        print(\"Cleanup running\")\n\n# Run 10 tasks with max 3 concurrent\nasyncio.run(run_tasks([sample_task] * 10, max_concurrent=3))\n```\n\nIf you Ctrl+C during execution, you'll see all the cleanup code run before the process exits.","ttft_ms":20717,"type":"result","duration_ms":24516,"uuid":"0109632b-67fb-47f8-8fee-74a134cd4ccf","ttft_stream_ms":964,"time_to_request_ms":43,"queued_turn_count":0}
